From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:43:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] feat(shader): split the T# Phi of an image store as for
 reads

An image_store whose T# came from one of two s_load_dwordx8 on either
side of a branch stopped with "GetImageResource dword 0 is not a valid
runtime value; chain: Phi(ReadConst(GetSrtResource), ReadConst(...))".
Reads through such a Phi are split into one read per incoming T# and a
select of their results; stores were not candidates, since running every
copy would store through every T#.

A store is now split the same way, and each copy stores only in the
lanes whose edge picked its T#: the copy's EXEC operand is ANDed with
that arm's condition and the negation of every earlier arm's. Atomics
through such a T# are still refused.

Tested: tests/DescriptorSelectionTests.cpp compiles a store through a
T# picked by s_cbranch_vccnz between two table slots; it stops with the
old error without the change, and with it the module validates and holds
two OpImageWrite. With the previous commit, 11 of the 12 compute shaders
of a retail title that stopped so now compile and validate (offline, no
guest memory).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
